title: 'c2c restart-stale: rolling restart of managed instances on old binaries'
updated_at: "2026-07-12T09:37:21Z"
---
After building/installing a new c2c version, running managed instances keep executing the OLD binary until manually restarted (see the just install-all warning: "live process(es) hold binaries about to be replaced ... will not auto-pick-up the new binary"). Add a single explicit command, `c2c restart-stale`, that identifies managed instances running an older installed binary and restarts them sequentially.

MOTIVATION
- Today the operator must eyeball the install warning, run `c2c instances`, and `c2c restart <name>` for each session by hand. Easy to forget; leaves the swarm split across binary versions (a known source of routing/feature-visibility bugs — new broker tools/flags are invisible until restart per CLAUDE.md).
- The upgrade path should be one command, ideally wired so `just install-all` / `just bi` can optionally trigger it.

SCOPE DECISION (2026-07-12)
- This is a rolling, best-effort restart command, not a claim of seamless hot upgrade.
- Include the coordinator by default. `--exclude-coordinator` is the opt-out; coordinator-specific behavior is no longer central to normal operation.
- Codex app-server is a first-class required path: preserve/resume the existing Codex thread, preserve inbox/ingress ledger correctness, and verify with a real managed Codex app-server session in tmux.
- `just install` is the primary install spelling and aliases `install-all`; after a successful interactive install, prompt whether to run `c2c restart-stale`. Non-interactive installs must never block on a prompt and must print the explicit follow-up command instead.
- Deeper seamless/idle-state work is tracked separately as a follow-up idea rather than expanding this slice.
- B153 is the prerequisite Codex lifecycle seam: app-server sessions currently lack normal config/PID enumeration, cannot use `c2c restart`, and do not reliably persist the late-discovered thread ID.

DESIGN CONSTRAINTS:
1. Naive sweep-restart: enumerate managed instances (`c2c instances`), `c2c restart <name>` each. Simple, but each restart drops the session transcript/context and interrupts any in-flight turn. NOT seamless — disruptive to active agents.
2. Signal-based hot reconnect: SIGUSR1 to the inner MCP/opencode pid reconnects the MCP session to the broker WITHOUT a full restart (CLAUDE.md documents SIGUSR1-to-inner-pid recovery). This refreshes the broker connection but does NOT swap the on-disk binary the process already exec`d — so it does not actually upgrade code, only re-establishes signals. Need to confirm what a SIGUSR1 reconnect can vs cannot pick up.
3. Generic idle gating is NOT part of this slice. The current cross-client activity timestamp is a heuristic, not authoritative proof that a turn has finished.
4. Staged/rolling restart: restart one instance at a time so the swarm never fully goes dark; coordinator restarts last. Preserves swarm liveness during the upgrade.
5. Version-aware skip: only restart instances whose running binary SHA != installed SHA (compare `/proc/<pid>/exe` target or the build-SHA the process reports) — avoid needless restarts. `c2c-install-live-holders.sh` already detects live holders; extend it to report per-instance running version.

OPEN QUESTIONS
- Can a running managed session actually adopt a new binary without re-exec? (If not, "restart" is unavoidable and "seamless" reduces to "graceful + rolling + idle-gated".)
- Command name and location are decided: `c2c restart-stale`. Coordinator is included by default; `--exclude-coordinator` opts out.
- Interaction with `c2c-install-live-holders.sh` (already enumerates holders) — reuse its detection.
- The command itself is explicit. The post-install integration prompts only on an interactive terminal and otherwise does not restart automatically.

ACCEPTANCE (first cut, subject to design)
- One command restarts all version-mismatched managed instances onto the installed binary.
- Rolling/sequential by default, continuing after individual failures and reporting restarted / skipped / failed instances.
- Coordinator included normally; `--exclude-coordinator` skips it.
- Codex app-server resumes the same thread/session and preserves ingress-ledger/inbox correctness, verified in a real tmux-managed session.
- `--dry-run` reports exactly what would restart without changing process state.
- Stale detection uses persisted launcher PID/start-time plus executable device/inode as a cheap same-inode fast path. When the inode differs, hash the installed binary once and `/proc/<pid>/exe` once per distinct running inode. Unknown/unreadable process identity skips safely unless explicitly forced.
- `just install` / `just install-all`, after a successful install on an interactive TTY, prompt whether to run `c2c restart-stale`; non-interactive runs never prompt or restart implicitly.
- Reports what it restarted, what it skipped, and any that failed.

Discovered from: 2026-07-12 `just install-all` run leaving 2 live c2c-mcp-server procs on the old binary; related CLAUDE.md notes on restart-after-broker-update and SIGUSR1-to-inner-pid.

DESIGN SYNTHESIS (2026-07-12): full write-up in `.collab/design/2026-07-12-c2c-client-upgrade-restart.md`. B145 (the detached Kimi notifier surviving restart) was discovered during intake and is already fixed; it is not a dependency of I010.
